---
title: How to Set Up Basic Search Parameters
---
NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Learn how to add type-safe, production-ready search parameters to your TanStack Router routes using schema validation. This guide covers the fundamentals of search parameter validation, reading values, and handling different data types with any standard schema-compliant validation library."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"quick-start","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Quick Start"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Set up search parameters with schema validation (recommended for production):"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nconst productSearchSchema = z.object({\n  page: z.number().default(1).catch(1),\n  category: z.string().default('all').catch('all'),\n  showSale: z.boolean().default(false).catch(false),\n})\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/products')({\n  validateSearch: productSearchSchema,\n  component: ProductsPage,\n})\n\nfunction ProductsPage() {\n  const { page, category, showSale } = Route.useSearch()\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <h1>Products</h1>\n      <p>Page: {page}</p>\n      <p>Category: {category}</p>\n      <p>Show Sale Items: {showSale ? 'Yes' : 'No'}</p>\n    </div>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"why-use-schema-validation-for-search-parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Why Use Schema Validation for Search Parameters?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Production Benefits:"}]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Safety"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Automatic TypeScript inference"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Runtime Validation"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Catches invalid URL parameters gracefully"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Default Values"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Fallback handling for missing parameters"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Error Handling"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Built-in validation error management"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Maintainability"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Clear, declarative schema definitions"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"validation-library-setup","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Validation Library Setup"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Router supports any standard schema-compliant validation library. This guide focuses on Zod for examples, but you can use any validation library."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Using Zod v4:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { z } from 'zod'\n\nconst searchSchema = z.object({\n  page: z.number().default(1),\n  category: z.string().default('all').catch('all'),\n})\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/products')({\n  validateSearch: searchSchema,\n  component: ProductsPage,\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For Zod v3:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"npm install zod @tanstack/zod-adapter","lang":"bash"},{"type":"code","value":"import { zodValidator, fallback } from '@tanstack/zod-adapter'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nconst searchSchema = z.object({\n  page: fallback(z.number(), 1).default(1),\n  category: fallback(z.string(), 'all').default('all'),\n})\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/products')({\n  validateSearch: zodValidator(searchSchema),\n  component: ProductsPage,\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For detailed validation library comparisons and advanced validation patterns, see:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"link","href":"./validate-search-params.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Validate Search Parameters with Schemas"}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"step-by-step-setup-with-zod","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Step-by-Step Setup with Zod"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The rest of this guide uses Zod v4 for examples, but the patterns apply to any validation library."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"step-1-define-your-search-schema","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Step 1: Define Your Search Schema"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Start by identifying what search parameters your route needs:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { z } from 'zod'\n\nconst shopSearchSchema = z.object({\n  // Pagination\n  page: z.number().default(1),\n  limit: z.number().default(20),\n\n  // Filtering\n  category: z.string().default('all'),\n  minPrice: z.number().default(0),\n  maxPrice: z.number().default(1000),\n\n  // Settings\n  sort: z.enum(['name', 'price', 'date']).default('name'),\n  ascending: z.boolean().default(true),\n\n  // Optional parameters\n  searchTerm: z.string().optional(),\n  showOnlyInStock: z.boolean().default(false),\n})\n\ntype ShopSearch = z.infer<typeof shopSearchSchema>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"step-2-add-schema-validation-to-route","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Step 2: Add Schema Validation to Route"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Connect your schema to the route:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"export const Route = createFileRoute('/shop')({\n  validateSearch: shopSearchSchema,\n  component: ShopPage,\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"step-3-read-search-parameters-in-components","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Step 3: Read Search Parameters in Components"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use the route's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useSearch()"},{"type":"text","value":" hook to access validated and typed search parameters:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"function ShopPage() {\n  const searchParams = Route.useSearch()\n\n  // All properties are fully type-safe and validated\n  const {\n    page,\n    limit,\n    category,\n    sort,\n    ascending,\n    searchTerm,\n    showOnlyInStock,\n  } = searchParams\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <h1>Shop - Page {page}</h1>\n      <div>Category: {category}</div>\n      <div>\n        Sort: {sort} ({ascending ? 'ascending' : 'descending'})\n      </div>\n      <div>Items per page: {limit}</div>\n      <div>In stock only: {showOnlyInStock ? 'Yes' : 'No'}</div>\n      {searchTerm && <div>Search: \"{searchTerm}\"</div>}\n    </div>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"common-search-parameter-patterns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Common Search Parameter Patterns"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"pagination-with-constraints","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pagination with Constraints"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const paginationSchema = z.object({\n  page: z.number().min(1).default(1),\n  limit: z.number().min(10).max(100).default(20),\n})\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts')({\n  validateSearch: paginationSchema,\n  component: PostsPage,\n})\n\nfunction PostsPage() {\n  const { page, limit } = Route.useSearch()\n\n  // Calculate offset for API calls\n  const offset = (page - 1) * limit\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <h1>Posts (Page {page})</h1>\n      <p>Showing {limit} posts per page</p>\n      <p>Offset: {offset}</p>\n      {/* Render posts... */}\n    </div>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"enum-validation-with-defaults","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Enum Validation with Defaults"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const catalogSchema = z.object({\n  sort: z.enum(['name', 'date', 'price']).default('name'),\n  category: z.enum(['electronics', 'clothing', 'books', 'all']).default('all'),\n  ascending: z.boolean().default(true),\n})\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/catalog')({\n  validateSearch: catalogSchema,\n  component: CatalogPage,\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"complex-data-types","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Complex Data Types"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const dashboardSchema = z.object({\n  // Numbers with validation\n  userId: z.number().positive().default(1),\n  refreshInterval: z.number().min(1000).max(60000).default(5000),\n\n  // Strings with validation\n  theme: z.enum(['light', 'dark']).default('light'),\n  timezone: z.string().optional(),\n\n  // Arrays with validation\n  selectedIds: z.number().array().default([]),\n  tags: z.string().array().default([]),\n\n  // Objects with validation\n  filters: z\n    .object({\n      status: z.enum(['active', 'inactive']).optional(),\n      type: z.string().optional(),\n    })\n    .prefault({}),\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"date-and-advanced-types","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Date and Advanced Types"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const reportSchema = z.object({\n  startDate: z.string().pipe(z.coerce.date()).optional(),\n  endDate: z.string().pipe(z.coerce.date()).optional(),\n  format: z.enum(['pdf', 'csv', 'excel']).default('pdf').catch('pdf'),\n  includeCharts: z.boolean().default(true),\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"reading-search-parameters-outside-components","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reading Search Parameters Outside Components"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"using-getrouteapi","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Using getRouteApi"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For code-split components or separate files:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// components/ProductFilters.tsx\nimport { getRouteApi } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nconst routeApi = getRouteApi('/products')\n\nexport function ProductFilters() {\n  const { category, sort, showSale } = routeApi.useSearch()\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <select value={category}>\n        <option value=\"all\">All Categories</option>\n        <option value=\"electronics\">Electronics</option>\n        <option value=\"clothing\">Clothing</option>\n      </select>\n      {/* More filters... */}\n    </div>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"using-usesearch-with-from","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Using useSearch with from"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useSearch } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nfunction GenericSearchDisplay() {\n  const search = useSearch({ from: '/products' })\n\n  return <div>Current filters: {JSON.stringify(search, null, 2)}</div>\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"manual-validation-understanding-the-primitives","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Manual Validation (Understanding the Primitives)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"While schema validation is recommended for production, understanding manual validation helps you understand how search parameters work under the hood:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// Educational example - use schema validation for production\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/example')({\n  validateSearch: (search: Record<string, unknown>) => ({\n    // Numbers need coercion from URL strings\n    page: Number(search.page) || 1,\n\n    // Strings can be cast with defaults\n    category: (search.category as string) || 'all',\n\n    // Booleans: TanStack Router auto-converts \"true\"/\"false\" to booleans\n    showSale: Boolean(search.showSale),\n\n    // Arrays need JSON parsing validation\n    selectedIds: Array.isArray(search.selectedIds)\n      ? search.selectedIds.map(Number).filter(Boolean)\n      : [],\n  }),\n  component: ExamplePage,\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"production-checklist","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Production Checklist"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use schema validation"}]},{"type":"text","value":" with a validation library for type safety and runtime validation"}]}],"checked":true},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Add fallback values"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for graceful error handling"}]}],"checked":true},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Set default values"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for optional parameters"}]}],"checked":true},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Validate constraints"}]},{"type":"text","value":" using your validation library's built-in validators"}]}],"checked":true},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Handle optional parameters"}]},{"type":"text","value":" appropriately"}]}],"checked":true},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type inference"}]},{"type":"text","value":" works automatically with proper schema setup"}]}],"checked":true},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Error boundaries"}]},{"type":"text","value":" are configured to handle validation failures"}]}],"checked":true}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"common-problems","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Common Problems"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"problem-search-parameters-cause-typescript-errors","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Problem: Search Parameters Cause TypeScript Errors"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cause:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" Missing or incorrect schema definition."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Solution:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" Ensure your schema covers all search parameters and use proper types:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// ❌ Missing schema or incorrect types\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/page')({\n  component: MyPage,\n})\n\n// ✅ Complete schema with proper validation\nconst searchSchema = z.object({\n  page: z.number().default(1).catch(1),\n  category: z.string().default('all').catch('all'),\n})\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/page')({\n  validateSearch: searchSchema,\n  component: MyPage,\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"problem-invalid-url-parameters-break-the-app","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Problem: Invalid URL Parameters Break the App"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cause:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" Not using fallback handling for error cases."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Solution:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" Use fallback values to provide safe defaults:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// ❌ No fallback handling\nconst schema = z.object({\n  page: z.number().default(1), // Will throw on invalid input\n})\n\n// ✅ Graceful fallback handling\nconst schema = z.object({\n  page: z.number().default(1).catch(1), // Safe fallback to 1\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"problem-optional-parameters-are-required-by-typescript","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Problem: Optional Parameters Are Required by TypeScript"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cause:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" Using "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".default()"},{"type":"text","value":" makes parameters required in navigation."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Solution:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".optional()"},{"type":"text","value":" for truly optional parameters:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const schema = z.object({\n  // Required with default (navigation can omit, but always present in component)\n  page: z.number().default(1).catch(1),\n\n  // Truly optional (can be undefined in component)\n  searchTerm: z.string().optional(),\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"problem-complex-objects-not-validating","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Problem: Complex Objects Not Validating"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cause:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" Nested objects need explicit schema definition."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Solution:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" Define complete nested schemas:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const schema = z.object({\n  filters: z\n    .object({\n      status: z.enum(['active', 'inactive']).optional(),\n      tags: z.string().array().optional(),\n      dateRange: z\n        .object({\n          start: z.string().pipe(z.coerce.date()),\n          end: z.string().pipe(z.coerce.date()),\n        })\n        .optional(),\n    })\n    .prefault({})\n    .catch({}),\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"common-next-steps","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Common Next Steps"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"After setting up basic search parameters, you might want to:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./validate-search-params.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Validate Search Parameters with Schemas"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Add robust validation with Zod, Valibot, or ArkType"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./navigate-with-search-params.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Navigate with Search Parameters"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Learn to update search params with Links and navigation"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./arrays-objects-dates-search-params.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Work with Arrays, Objects, and Dates"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Handle arrays, objects, dates, and nested data structures"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"related-resources","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Related Resources"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Validation Libraries:"}]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"https://zod.dev/","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Zod Documentation"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Complete validation library reference"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"https://valibot.dev/","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Valibot Documentation"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Lightweight validation library"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/jquense/yup","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Yup Documentation"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Object schema validation"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Router:"}]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"https://tanstack.com/router/latest/docs/framework/react/api/router/zodValidator","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Zod Adapter"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Official Zod adapter"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"https://tanstack.com/router/latest/docs/framework/react/api/router/valibotValidator","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Valibot Adapter"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Official Valibot adapter"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../guide/search-params.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Search Parameters Guide"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Comprehensive search parameters documentation"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../guide/type-safety.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Safety Guide"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Understanding TanStack Router's type safety"}]}]}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"quick-start","text":"Quick Start","level":2},{"id":"why-use-schema-validation-for-search-parameters","text":"Why Use Schema Validation for Search Parameters?","level":2},{"id":"validation-library-setup","text":"Validation Library Setup","level":2},{"id":"step-by-step-setup-with-zod","text":"Step-by-Step Setup with Zod","level":2},{"id":"step-1-define-your-search-schema","text":"Step 1: Define Your Search Schema","level":3},{"id":"step-2-add-schema-validation-to-route","text":"Step 2: Add Schema Validation to Route","level":3},{"id":"step-3-read-search-parameters-in-components","text":"Step 3: Read Search Parameters in Components","level":3},{"id":"common-search-parameter-patterns","text":"Common Search Parameter Patterns","level":2},{"id":"pagination-with-constraints","text":"Pagination with Constraints","level":3},{"id":"enum-validation-with-defaults","text":"Enum Validation with Defaults","level":3},{"id":"complex-data-types","text":"Complex Data Types","level":3},{"id":"date-and-advanced-types","text":"Date and Advanced Types","level":3},{"id":"reading-search-parameters-outside-components","text":"Reading Search Parameters Outside Components","level":2},{"id":"using-getrouteapi","text":"Using getRouteApi","level":3},{"id":"using-usesearch-with-from","text":"Using useSearch with from","level":3},{"id":"manual-validation-understanding-the-primitives","text":"Manual Validation (Understanding the Primitives)","level":2},{"id":"production-checklist","text":"Production Checklist","level":2},{"id":"common-problems","text":"Common Problems","level":2},{"id":"problem-search-parameters-cause-typescript-errors","text":"Problem: Search Parameters Cause TypeScript Errors","level":3},{"id":"problem-invalid-url-parameters-break-the-app","text":"Problem: Invalid URL Parameters Break the App","level":3},{"id":"problem-optional-parameters-are-required-by-typescript","text":"Problem: Optional Parameters Are Required by TypeScript","level":3},{"id":"problem-complex-objects-not-validating","text":"Problem: Complex Objects Not Validating","level":3},{"id":"common-next-steps","text":"Common Next Steps","level":2},{"id":"related-resources","text":"Related Resources","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nLearn how to add type-safe, production-ready search parameters to your TanStack Router routes using schema validation. This guide covers the fundamentals of search parameter validation, reading values, and handling different data types with any standard schema-compliant validation library.\n\n## Quick Start\n\nSet up search parameters with schema validation (recommended for production):\n\n```tsx\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nconst productSearchSchema = z.object({\n  page: z.number().default(1).catch(1),\n  category: z.string().default('all').catch('all'),\n  showSale: z.boolean().default(false).catch(false),\n})\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/products')({\n  validateSearch: productSearchSchema,\n  component: ProductsPage,\n})\n\nfunction ProductsPage() {\n  const { page, category, showSale } = Route.useSearch()\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <h1>Products</h1>\n      <p>Page: {page}</p>\n      <p>Category: {category}</p>\n      <p>Show Sale Items: {showSale ? 'Yes' : 'No'}</p>\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n## Why Use Schema Validation for Search Parameters?\n\n**Production Benefits:**\n\n- **Type Safety**: Automatic TypeScript inference\n- **Runtime Validation**: Catches invalid URL parameters gracefully\n- **Default Values**: Fallback handling for missing parameters\n- **Error Handling**: Built-in validation error management\n- **Maintainability**: Clear, declarative schema definitions\n\n## Validation Library Setup\n\nTanStack Router supports any standard schema-compliant validation library. This guide focuses on Zod for examples, but you can use any validation library.\n\nUsing Zod v4:\n\n```tsx\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nconst searchSchema = z.object({\n  page: z.number().default(1),\n  category: z.string().default('all').catch('all'),\n})\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/products')({\n  validateSearch: searchSchema,\n  component: ProductsPage,\n})\n```\n\nFor Zod v3:\n\n```bash\nnpm install zod @tanstack/zod-adapter\n```\n\n```tsx\nimport { zodValidator, fallback } from '@tanstack/zod-adapter'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nconst searchSchema = z.object({\n  page: fallback(z.number(), 1).default(1),\n  category: fallback(z.string(), 'all').default('all'),\n})\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/products')({\n  validateSearch: zodValidator(searchSchema),\n  component: ProductsPage,\n})\n```\n\n**For detailed validation library comparisons and advanced validation patterns, see:** [Validate Search Parameters with Schemas](./validate-search-params.md)\n\n## Step-by-Step Setup with Zod\n\nThe rest of this guide uses Zod v4 for examples, but the patterns apply to any validation library.\n\n### Step 1: Define Your Search Schema\n\nStart by identifying what search parameters your route needs:\n\n```tsx\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nconst shopSearchSchema = z.object({\n  // Pagination\n  page: z.number().default(1),\n  limit: z.number().default(20),\n\n  // Filtering\n  category: z.string().default('all'),\n  minPrice: z.number().default(0),\n  maxPrice: z.number().default(1000),\n\n  // Settings\n  sort: z.enum(['name', 'price', 'date']).default('name'),\n  ascending: z.boolean().default(true),\n\n  // Optional parameters\n  searchTerm: z.string().optional(),\n  showOnlyInStock: z.boolean().default(false),\n})\n\ntype ShopSearch = z.infer<typeof shopSearchSchema>\n```\n\n### Step 2: Add Schema Validation to Route\n\nConnect your schema to the route:\n\n```tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/shop')({\n  validateSearch: shopSearchSchema,\n  component: ShopPage,\n})\n```\n\n### Step 3: Read Search Parameters in Components\n\nUse the route's `useSearch()` hook to access validated and typed search parameters:\n\n```tsx\nfunction ShopPage() {\n  const searchParams = Route.useSearch()\n\n  // All properties are fully type-safe and validated\n  const {\n    page,\n    limit,\n    category,\n    sort,\n    ascending,\n    searchTerm,\n    showOnlyInStock,\n  } = searchParams\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <h1>Shop - Page {page}</h1>\n      <div>Category: {category}</div>\n      <div>\n        Sort: {sort} ({ascending ? 'ascending' : 'descending'})\n      </div>\n      <div>Items per page: {limit}</div>\n      <div>In stock only: {showOnlyInStock ? 'Yes' : 'No'}</div>\n      {searchTerm && <div>Search: \"{searchTerm}\"</div>}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n## Common Search Parameter Patterns\n\n### Pagination with Constraints\n\n```tsx\nconst paginationSchema = z.object({\n  page: z.number().min(1).default(1),\n  limit: z.number().min(10).max(100).default(20),\n})\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts')({\n  validateSearch: paginationSchema,\n  component: PostsPage,\n})\n\nfunction PostsPage() {\n  const { page, limit } = Route.useSearch()\n\n  // Calculate offset for API calls\n  const offset = (page - 1) * limit\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <h1>Posts (Page {page})</h1>\n      <p>Showing {limit} posts per page</p>\n      <p>Offset: {offset}</p>\n      {/* Render posts... */}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n### Enum Validation with Defaults\n\n```tsx\nconst catalogSchema = z.object({\n  sort: z.enum(['name', 'date', 'price']).default('name'),\n  category: z.enum(['electronics', 'clothing', 'books', 'all']).default('all'),\n  ascending: z.boolean().default(true),\n})\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/catalog')({\n  validateSearch: catalogSchema,\n  component: CatalogPage,\n})\n```\n\n### Complex Data Types\n\n```tsx\nconst dashboardSchema = z.object({\n  // Numbers with validation\n  userId: z.number().positive().default(1),\n  refreshInterval: z.number().min(1000).max(60000).default(5000),\n\n  // Strings with validation\n  theme: z.enum(['light', 'dark']).default('light'),\n  timezone: z.string().optional(),\n\n  // Arrays with validation\n  selectedIds: z.number().array().default([]),\n  tags: z.string().array().default([]),\n\n  // Objects with validation\n  filters: z\n    .object({\n      status: z.enum(['active', 'inactive']).optional(),\n      type: z.string().optional(),\n    })\n    .prefault({}),\n})\n```\n\n### Date and Advanced Types\n\n```tsx\nconst reportSchema = z.object({\n  startDate: z.string().pipe(z.coerce.date()).optional(),\n  endDate: z.string().pipe(z.coerce.date()).optional(),\n  format: z.enum(['pdf', 'csv', 'excel']).default('pdf').catch('pdf'),\n  includeCharts: z.boolean().default(true),\n})\n```\n\n## Reading Search Parameters Outside Components\n\n### Using getRouteApi\n\nFor code-split components or separate files:\n\n```tsx\n// components/ProductFilters.tsx\nimport { getRouteApi } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nconst routeApi = getRouteApi('/products')\n\nexport function ProductFilters() {\n  const { category, sort, showSale } = routeApi.useSearch()\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <select value={category}>\n        <option value=\"all\">All Categories</option>\n        <option value=\"electronics\">Electronics</option>\n        <option value=\"clothing\">Clothing</option>\n      </select>\n      {/* More filters... */}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n### Using useSearch with from\n\n```tsx\nimport { useSearch } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nfunction GenericSearchDisplay() {\n  const search = useSearch({ from: '/products' })\n\n  return <div>Current filters: {JSON.stringify(search, null, 2)}</div>\n}\n```\n\n## Manual Validation (Understanding the Primitives)\n\nWhile schema validation is recommended for production, understanding manual validation helps you understand how search parameters work under the hood:\n\n```tsx\n// Educational example - use schema validation for production\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/example')({\n  validateSearch: (search: Record<string, unknown>) => ({\n    // Numbers need coercion from URL strings\n    page: Number(search.page) || 1,\n\n    // Strings can be cast with defaults\n    category: (search.category as string) || 'all',\n\n    // Booleans: TanStack Router auto-converts \"true\"/\"false\" to booleans\n    showSale: Boolean(search.showSale),\n\n    // Arrays need JSON parsing validation\n    selectedIds: Array.isArray(search.selectedIds)\n      ? search.selectedIds.map(Number).filter(Boolean)\n      : [],\n  }),\n  component: ExamplePage,\n})\n```\n\n## Production Checklist\n\n- [x] **Use schema validation** with a validation library for type safety and runtime validation\n- [x] **Add fallback values** for graceful error handling\n- [x] **Set default values** for optional parameters\n- [x] **Validate constraints** using your validation library's built-in validators\n- [x] **Handle optional parameters** appropriately\n- [x] **Type inference** works automatically with proper schema setup\n- [x] **Error boundaries** are configured to handle validation failures\n\n## Common Problems\n\n### Problem: Search Parameters Cause TypeScript Errors\n\n**Cause:** Missing or incorrect schema definition.\n\n**Solution:** Ensure your schema covers all search parameters and use proper types:\n\n```tsx\n// ❌ Missing schema or incorrect types\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/page')({\n  component: MyPage,\n})\n\n// ✅ Complete schema with proper validation\nconst searchSchema = z.object({\n  page: z.number().default(1).catch(1),\n  category: z.string().default('all').catch('all'),\n})\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/page')({\n  validateSearch: searchSchema,\n  component: MyPage,\n})\n```\n\n### Problem: Invalid URL Parameters Break the App\n\n**Cause:** Not using fallback handling for error cases.\n\n**Solution:** Use fallback values to provide safe defaults:\n\n```tsx\n// ❌ No fallback handling\nconst schema = z.object({\n  page: z.number().default(1), // Will throw on invalid input\n})\n\n// ✅ Graceful fallback handling\nconst schema = z.object({\n  page: z.number().default(1).catch(1), // Safe fallback to 1\n})\n```\n\n### Problem: Optional Parameters Are Required by TypeScript\n\n**Cause:** Using `.default()` makes parameters required in navigation.\n\n**Solution:** Use `.optional()` for truly optional parameters:\n\n```tsx\nconst schema = z.object({\n  // Required with default (navigation can omit, but always present in component)\n  page: z.number().default(1).catch(1),\n\n  // Truly optional (can be undefined in component)\n  searchTerm: z.string().optional(),\n})\n```\n\n### Problem: Complex Objects Not Validating\n\n**Cause:** Nested objects need explicit schema definition.\n\n**Solution:** Define complete nested schemas:\n\n```tsx\nconst schema = z.object({\n  filters: z\n    .object({\n      status: z.enum(['active', 'inactive']).optional(),\n      tags: z.string().array().optional(),\n      dateRange: z\n        .object({\n          start: z.string().pipe(z.coerce.date()),\n          end: z.string().pipe(z.coerce.date()),\n        })\n        .optional(),\n    })\n    .prefault({})\n    .catch({}),\n})\n```\n\n## Common Next Steps\n\nAfter setting up basic search parameters, you might want to:\n\n- [Validate Search Parameters with Schemas](./validate-search-params.md) - Add robust validation with Zod, Valibot, or ArkType\n- [Navigate with Search Parameters](./navigate-with-search-params.md) - Learn to update search params with Links and navigation\n- [Work with Arrays, Objects, and Dates](./arrays-objects-dates-search-params.md) - Handle arrays, objects, dates, and nested data structures\n\n## Related Resources\n\n- **Validation Libraries:**\n  - [Zod Documentation](https://zod.dev/) - Complete validation library reference\n  - [Valibot Documentation](https://valibot.dev/) - Lightweight validation library\n  - [Yup Documentation](https://github.com/jquense/yup) - Object schema validation\n- **TanStack Router:**\n  - [TanStack Zod Adapter](https://tanstack.com/router/latest/docs/framework/react/api/router/zodValidator) - Official Zod adapter\n  - [TanStack Valibot Adapter](https://tanstack.com/router/latest/docs/framework/react/api/router/valibotValidator) - Official Valibot adapter\n  - [Search Parameters Guide](../guide/search-params.md) - Comprehensive search parameters documentation\n  - [Type Safety Guide](../guide/type-safety.md) - Understanding TanStack Router's type safety\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: How to Set Up Basic Search Parameters\n---\n\nLearn how to add type-safe, production-ready search parameters to your TanStack Router routes using schema validation. This guide covers the fundamentals of search parameter validation, reading values, and handling different data types with any standard schema-compliant validation library.\n\n## Quick Start\n\nSet up search parameters with schema validation (recommended for production):\n\n```tsx\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nconst productSearchSchema = z.object({\n  page: z.number().default(1).catch(1),\n  category: z.string().default('all').catch('all'),\n  showSale: z.boolean().default(false).catch(false),\n})\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/products')({\n  validateSearch: productSearchSchema,\n  component: ProductsPage,\n})\n\nfunction ProductsPage() {\n  const { page, category, showSale } = Route.useSearch()\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <h1>Products</h1>\n      <p>Page: {page}</p>\n      <p>Category: {category}</p>\n      <p>Show Sale Items: {showSale ? 'Yes' : 'No'}</p>\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n## Why Use Schema Validation for Search Parameters?\n\n**Production Benefits:**\n\n- **Type Safety**: Automatic TypeScript inference\n- **Runtime Validation**: Catches invalid URL parameters gracefully\n- **Default Values**: Fallback handling for missing parameters\n- **Error Handling**: Built-in validation error management\n- **Maintainability**: Clear, declarative schema definitions\n\n## Validation Library Setup\n\nTanStack Router supports any standard schema-compliant validation library. This guide focuses on Zod for examples, but you can use any validation library.\n\nUsing Zod v4:\n\n```tsx\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nconst searchSchema = z.object({\n  page: z.number().default(1),\n  category: z.string().default('all').catch('all'),\n})\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/products')({\n  validateSearch: searchSchema,\n  component: ProductsPage,\n})\n```\n\nFor Zod v3:\n\n```bash\nnpm install zod @tanstack/zod-adapter\n```\n\n```tsx\nimport { zodValidator, fallback } from '@tanstack/zod-adapter'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nconst searchSchema = z.object({\n  page: fallback(z.number(), 1).default(1),\n  category: fallback(z.string(), 'all').default('all'),\n})\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/products')({\n  validateSearch: zodValidator(searchSchema),\n  component: ProductsPage,\n})\n```\n\n**For detailed validation library comparisons and advanced validation patterns, see:** [Validate Search Parameters with Schemas](./validate-search-params.md)\n\n## Step-by-Step Setup with Zod\n\nThe rest of this guide uses Zod v4 for examples, but the patterns apply to any validation library.\n\n### Step 1: Define Your Search Schema\n\nStart by identifying what search parameters your route needs:\n\n```tsx\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nconst shopSearchSchema = z.object({\n  // Pagination\n  page: z.number().default(1),\n  limit: z.number().default(20),\n\n  // Filtering\n  category: z.string().default('all'),\n  minPrice: z.number().default(0),\n  maxPrice: z.number().default(1000),\n\n  // Settings\n  sort: z.enum(['name', 'price', 'date']).default('name'),\n  ascending: z.boolean().default(true),\n\n  // Optional parameters\n  searchTerm: z.string().optional(),\n  showOnlyInStock: z.boolean().default(false),\n})\n\ntype ShopSearch = z.infer<typeof shopSearchSchema>\n```\n\n### Step 2: Add Schema Validation to Route\n\nConnect your schema to the route:\n\n```tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/shop')({\n  validateSearch: shopSearchSchema,\n  component: ShopPage,\n})\n```\n\n### Step 3: Read Search Parameters in Components\n\nUse the route's `useSearch()` hook to access validated and typed search parameters:\n\n```tsx\nfunction ShopPage() {\n  const searchParams = Route.useSearch()\n\n  // All properties are fully type-safe and validated\n  const {\n    page,\n    limit,\n    category,\n    sort,\n    ascending,\n    searchTerm,\n    showOnlyInStock,\n  } = searchParams\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <h1>Shop - Page {page}</h1>\n      <div>Category: {category}</div>\n      <div>\n        Sort: {sort} ({ascending ? 'ascending' : 'descending'})\n      </div>\n      <div>Items per page: {limit}</div>\n      <div>In stock only: {showOnlyInStock ? 'Yes' : 'No'}</div>\n      {searchTerm && <div>Search: \"{searchTerm}\"</div>}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n## Common Search Parameter Patterns\n\n### Pagination with Constraints\n\n```tsx\nconst paginationSchema = z.object({\n  page: z.number().min(1).default(1),\n  limit: z.number().min(10).max(100).default(20),\n})\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts')({\n  validateSearch: paginationSchema,\n  component: PostsPage,\n})\n\nfunction PostsPage() {\n  const { page, limit } = Route.useSearch()\n\n  // Calculate offset for API calls\n  const offset = (page - 1) * limit\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <h1>Posts (Page {page})</h1>\n      <p>Showing {limit} posts per page</p>\n      <p>Offset: {offset}</p>\n      {/* Render posts... */}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n### Enum Validation with Defaults\n\n```tsx\nconst catalogSchema = z.object({\n  sort: z.enum(['name', 'date', 'price']).default('name'),\n  category: z.enum(['electronics', 'clothing', 'books', 'all']).default('all'),\n  ascending: z.boolean().default(true),\n})\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/catalog')({\n  validateSearch: catalogSchema,\n  component: CatalogPage,\n})\n```\n\n### Complex Data Types\n\n```tsx\nconst dashboardSchema = z.object({\n  // Numbers with validation\n  userId: z.number().positive().default(1),\n  refreshInterval: z.number().min(1000).max(60000).default(5000),\n\n  // Strings with validation\n  theme: z.enum(['light', 'dark']).default('light'),\n  timezone: z.string().optional(),\n\n  // Arrays with validation\n  selectedIds: z.number().array().default([]),\n  tags: z.string().array().default([]),\n\n  // Objects with validation\n  filters: z\n    .object({\n      status: z.enum(['active', 'inactive']).optional(),\n      type: z.string().optional(),\n    })\n    .prefault({}),\n})\n```\n\n### Date and Advanced Types\n\n```tsx\nconst reportSchema = z.object({\n  startDate: z.string().pipe(z.coerce.date()).optional(),\n  endDate: z.string().pipe(z.coerce.date()).optional(),\n  format: z.enum(['pdf', 'csv', 'excel']).default('pdf').catch('pdf'),\n  includeCharts: z.boolean().default(true),\n})\n```\n\n## Reading Search Parameters Outside Components\n\n### Using getRouteApi\n\nFor code-split components or separate files:\n\n```tsx\n// components/ProductFilters.tsx\nimport { getRouteApi } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nconst routeApi = getRouteApi('/products')\n\nexport function ProductFilters() {\n  const { category, sort, showSale } = routeApi.useSearch()\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <select value={category}>\n        <option value=\"all\">All Categories</option>\n        <option value=\"electronics\">Electronics</option>\n        <option value=\"clothing\">Clothing</option>\n      </select>\n      {/* More filters... */}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n### Using useSearch with from\n\n```tsx\nimport { useSearch } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nfunction GenericSearchDisplay() {\n  const search = useSearch({ from: '/products' })\n\n  return <div>Current filters: {JSON.stringify(search, null, 2)}</div>\n}\n```\n\n## Manual Validation (Understanding the Primitives)\n\nWhile schema validation is recommended for production, understanding manual validation helps you understand how search parameters work under the hood:\n\n```tsx\n// Educational example - use schema validation for production\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/example')({\n  validateSearch: (search: Record<string, unknown>) => ({\n    // Numbers need coercion from URL strings\n    page: Number(search.page) || 1,\n\n    // Strings can be cast with defaults\n    category: (search.category as string) || 'all',\n\n    // Booleans: TanStack Router auto-converts \"true\"/\"false\" to booleans\n    showSale: Boolean(search.showSale),\n\n    // Arrays need JSON parsing validation\n    selectedIds: Array.isArray(search.selectedIds)\n      ? search.selectedIds.map(Number).filter(Boolean)\n      : [],\n  }),\n  component: ExamplePage,\n})\n```\n\n## Production Checklist\n\n- [x] **Use schema validation** with a validation library for type safety and runtime validation\n- [x] **Add fallback values** for graceful error handling\n- [x] **Set default values** for optional parameters\n- [x] **Validate constraints** using your validation library's built-in validators\n- [x] **Handle optional parameters** appropriately\n- [x] **Type inference** works automatically with proper schema setup\n- [x] **Error boundaries** are configured to handle validation failures\n\n## Common Problems\n\n### Problem: Search Parameters Cause TypeScript Errors\n\n**Cause:** Missing or incorrect schema definition.\n\n**Solution:** Ensure your schema covers all search parameters and use proper types:\n\n```tsx\n// ❌ Missing schema or incorrect types\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/page')({\n  component: MyPage,\n})\n\n// ✅ Complete schema with proper validation\nconst searchSchema = z.object({\n  page: z.number().default(1).catch(1),\n  category: z.string().default('all').catch('all'),\n})\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/page')({\n  validateSearch: searchSchema,\n  component: MyPage,\n})\n```\n\n### Problem: Invalid URL Parameters Break the App\n\n**Cause:** Not using fallback handling for error cases.\n\n**Solution:** Use fallback values to provide safe defaults:\n\n```tsx\n// ❌ No fallback handling\nconst schema = z.object({\n  page: z.number().default(1), // Will throw on invalid input\n})\n\n// ✅ Graceful fallback handling\nconst schema = z.object({\n  page: z.number().default(1).catch(1), // Safe fallback to 1\n})\n```\n\n### Problem: Optional Parameters Are Required by TypeScript\n\n**Cause:** Using `.default()` makes parameters required in navigation.\n\n**Solution:** Use `.optional()` for truly optional parameters:\n\n```tsx\nconst schema = z.object({\n  // Required with default (navigation can omit, but always present in component)\n  page: z.number().default(1).catch(1),\n\n  // Truly optional (can be undefined in component)\n  searchTerm: z.string().optional(),\n})\n```\n\n### Problem: Complex Objects Not Validating\n\n**Cause:** Nested objects need explicit schema definition.\n\n**Solution:** Define complete nested schemas:\n\n```tsx\nconst schema = z.object({\n  filters: z\n    .object({\n      status: z.enum(['active', 'inactive']).optional(),\n      tags: z.string().array().optional(),\n      dateRange: z\n        .object({\n          start: z.string().pipe(z.coerce.date()),\n          end: z.string().pipe(z.coerce.date()),\n        })\n        .optional(),\n    })\n    .prefault({})\n    .catch({}),\n})\n```\n\n## Common Next Steps\n\nAfter setting up basic search parameters, you might want to:\n\n- [Validate Search Parameters with Schemas](./validate-search-params.md) - Add robust validation with Zod, Valibot, or ArkType\n- [Navigate with Search Parameters](./navigate-with-search-params.md) - Learn to update search params with Links and navigation\n- [Work with Arrays, Objects, and Dates](./arrays-objects-dates-search-params.md) - Handle arrays, objects, dates, and nested data structures\n\n## Related Resources\n\n- **Validation Libraries:**\n  - [Zod Documentation](https://zod.dev/) - Complete validation library reference\n  - [Valibot Documentation](https://valibot.dev/) - Lightweight validation library\n  - [Yup Documentation](https://github.com/jquense/yup) - Object schema validation\n- **TanStack Router:**\n  - [TanStack Zod Adapter](https://tanstack.com/router/latest/docs/framework/react/api/router/zodValidator) - Official Zod adapter\n  - [TanStack Valibot Adapter](https://tanstack.com/router/latest/docs/framework/react/api/router/valibotValidator) - Official Valibot adapter\n  - [Search Parameters Guide](../guide/search-params.md) - Comprehensive search parameters documentation\n  - [Type Safety Guide](../guide/type-safety.md) - Understanding TanStack Router's type safety\n"}
